From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: the voice processor keeps rendering while the
 front end is trapped

The frame thread skipped the whole VP/DSP pipeline while FECTL's method
mode was TRAPPED or HALTED, and ran the monitor alone, so every
idle-voice trap was a gap of silence as long as the title's interrupt
took to resume the front end. In a level where voices start and stop
all the time (Crash's Arctic Antics), 13-23% of APU frames went out
empty in 150-260 gaps of up to 21 ms every 10 s: the music played in
fragments, at about half speed with repeats. A trap stops the method
queue, not the voice processor, so:

- The pipeline runs unless the front end is halted. FEMETHMODE is a
  field and TRAPPED (0xE0) holds HALTED's bit (0x80), so the old bit
  test also stopped it on a trap; the mode is now compared whole.
- While trapped, the VP's list walk doesn't report more idle voices
  (they would overwrite FEDECMETH/FEDECPARAM, which the ISR reads); they
  are reported on the first frame after the resume.

Loopback of the level, same deterministic attract demo: 921 and 933
dropouts and 1,083 and 1,011 clicks in 60 s before, 96 and 136 after;
the level music advances one second per second. The remaining gaps
are the front end's short halted spells (0.4-2.4% of frames), left as
they were. Beyond the 18.45 scope (monitor, pacing, resampler):
flagged in the Crash notes.

Never pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apu/apu_core.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 src/apu/apu_vp.c   |  9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apu/apu_core.c b/src/apu/apu_core.c
index 11539e2..5dd8a93 100644
--- a/src/apu/apu_core.c
+++ b/src/apu/apu_core.c
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ void mcpx_apu_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, uint64_t val,
          * successful DirectSound create, that hang is not confined to audio.
          *
          * Resume whenever the write is not switching the block off; the thread
-         * re-checks FECTL itself and idles again if it is halted or trapped. */
+         * re-checks FECTL itself and skips the pipeline while it is halted. */
         {
             uint32_t sectl = qatomic_read(&d->regs[NV_PAPU_SECTL]);
             uint32_t fectl = qatomic_read(&d->regs[NV_PAPU_FECTL]);
@@ -492,12 +492,20 @@ static void *mcpx_apu_frame_thread(void *arg)
          * The VP/DSP pipeline (se_frame) only runs when registers allow it. */
         throttle(d);
 
+        /* A trapped front end stops the method queue, not the voice
+         * processor: the VP keeps rendering the voices it has while the
+         * title's ISR handles the trap (and holds back further idle-voice
+         * methods, mcpx_apu_vp_frame). Skipping the whole frame there made
+         * every trap a gap of silence as long as the interrupt took: in a
+         * level with voices starting and stopping, 13-23% of frames in
+         * 150-260 gaps of up to 21 ms every 10 s. Halted still stops it.
+         * FEMETHMODE is a field, and TRAPPED (0xE0) holds HALTED's bit
+         * (0x80), so the mode is compared whole. */
         int xcntmode = GET_MASK(qatomic_read(&d->regs[NV_PAPU_SECTL]),
                                 NV_PAPU_SECTL_XCNTMODE);
         uint32_t fectl = qatomic_read(&d->regs[NV_PAPU_FECTL]);
         bool apu_active = (xcntmode != NV_PAPU_SECTL_XCNTMODE_OFF) &&
-                          !(fectl & NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE_TRAPPED) &&
-                          !(fectl & NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE_HALTED);
+                          (fectl & NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE) != NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE_HALTED;
 
         if (apu_active && !g_test_tone.active) {
             /* Full pipeline: VP voices → DSP → monitor → waveOut */
diff --git a/src/apu/apu_vp.c b/src/apu/apu_vp.c
index 4dd4452..02f7cde 100644
--- a/src/apu/apu_vp.c
+++ b/src/apu/apu_vp.c
@@ -1244,7 +1244,14 @@ void mcpx_apu_vp_frame(MCPXAPUState *d,
 
             if (!voice_get_mask(d, v, NV_PAVS_VOICE_PAR_STATE,
                                 NV_PAVS_VOICE_PAR_STATE_ACTIVE_VOICE)) {
-                fe_method(d, SE2FE_IDLE_VOICE, v);
+                /* While the front end is trapped the idle voice waits, as an
+                 * SE2FE method waits in the hardware's queue: reporting it
+                 * would overwrite the trapped method and handle the ISR is
+                 * about to read. It is reported on the first frame after the
+                 * resume. */
+                if ((d->regs[NV_PAPU_FECTL] & NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE)
+                        != NV_PAPU_FECTL_FEMETHMODE_TRAPPED)
+                    fe_method(d, SE2FE_IDLE_VOICE, v);
             } else {
                 /* Process voice directly (single-threaded) */
                 voice_process(d, mixbins, d->vp.sample_buf, v, list);
